{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"All 63 focused tests passed, with 479 assertions. The forced-retry reproduction executed one append request twice in a single `dial-step!` call, despite `:mirror-budget 1`. This issue predates S2a, but remains in the touched path and fails the explicit purity checkpoint. I’m recording a CHANGES REQUESTED verdict with that provenance and the reproduction."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; Path('\\\\''collab/1791355023304-stream-s2a-review.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md'\\\\'').write_text(\\\"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-07 06:39:20 GMT\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 13:39:20 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\nSession-ID: unavailable\\\\n\\\\n# Independent S2a review\\\\n\\\\n**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED**\\\\n\\\\nReviewed the uncommitted five-file diff in \"'`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`, branch `stream-crossmachine-s2`, HEAD `65f635d0`, against the S2 architect specification §1.1, §1.2, §2 and §3'\"'\\\\''s S2a plan, and mob consensus D1–D3/D5. No code, design, or test files were modified. Only this requested review artifact was written; no other worktree was accessed.\\\\n\\\\n## Blocking finding\\\\n\\\\n### R1 — P1: dial mirror effects execute inside an atom retry function\\\\n\\\\n**Location:** \"'`src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:587-590`; effect paths `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:235` and `:161-168`.'\"\\\\n\\\\n\"'`dial-step!` calls `remote/mirror-step` inside the function supplied to `swap! mirror-cursor`. That function reads streams, invokes source operations (including append!), and writes answers. If the cursor atom changes before the compare-and-set commits, swap! executes those effects again. The cursor transaction cannot roll back an already accepted source append or answer write.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThis fails the task'\\\\''s explicit checkpoint “Are all side-effects kept outside atom retry?” It also means the non-rewind branch for append\"'! does not by itself prevent duplicate execution through the dial composition. A retry can exceed a tick'\"'\\\\''s mirror budget.\\\\n\\\\n**Provenance:** This effectful swap\"'! already existed at HEAD. S2a changes its body to pass bounds but preserves the defect. This is an inherited defect in the specifically reviewed/touched path, not a claim that S2a introduced the retry hazard. The blocking verdict follows the requested purity checkpoint; the new remote loop itself otherwise passes the inspected requirements.'\"\\\\n\\\\n**Deterministic reproduction, executed without writing a test file:** construct the minimal dial state consumed by dial-step\"'!, with one append! request and mirror-budget 1. Wrap the real mirror-step to replace the cursor atom'\"'\\\\''s value after its first invocation with an equal cursor carrying different metadata. This changes object identity, forces the swap\"'! CAS to fail, and leaves the logical cursor unchanged. The wrapper performs no source append itself.'\"\\\\n\\\\nObserved:\\\\n\"'```clojure'\"\\\\n{:source-values [:once :once], :answer-count 2, :mirror-invocations 2}\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe following executable reproduction uses only the current implementations plus the stated CAS-conflict instrumentation:\\\\n\\\\n\"'```clojure'\"\\\\n(require '\\\\''[dao.stream :as s] '\\\\''[dao.stream.ringbuffer :as rb] '\\\\''[dao.stream.remote :as remote] '\\\\''[dao.stream.ws-project :as p])\\\\n(defn ring [] (:dao.stream/handle (rb/create\"'! {:dao.stream/type rb/transport-type rb/capacity-key 16})))'\"\\\\n(defn values [h] (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (s/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)) acc []] (let [r (s/next h c)] (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r))) acc))))\\\\n(let [source (ring) requests (ring) answers (ring) c (:dao.stream/cursor (s/cursor requests :dao.stream/oldest)) cursor-atom (atom c) dial (atom {:ring requests :table {\\\\\\\"w\\\\\\\" {:handle source :surface #{:writer}}} :channel (atom {:handle answers}) :mirror-cursor cursor-atom :mirror-budget 1}) step remote/mirror-step calls (atom 0)]\\\\n(s/append\"'! requests {:dao.stream/identity '\"\\\\\\\"w\\\\\\\" :dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append\"'! :dao.stream.remote/args [:once] :dao.stream.remote/id 1})'\"\\\\n(with-redefs [remote/mirror-step (fn [& args] (let [result (apply step args)] (when (= 1 (swap\"'! calls inc)) (reset! cursor-atom (with-meta @cursor-atom {:force-cas-retry true}))) result))] (p/dial-step! dial))'\"\\\\n(prn {:source-values (values source) :answer-count (count (values answers)) :mirror-invocations @calls}))\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\n\\\\nA separate two-driver overlap reproduction, synchronizing the first two mirror invocations after their effects and before cursor commits, also produced two source appends and two answer writes for the same request (three mirror invocations, the final retry reading blocked). This demonstrates the caller-overlap hazard in addition to the forced-retry mechanism.\\\\n\\\\n**Requested correction:** compute mirror effects outside atom retry and commit only the resulting cursor through a state-only operation. Follow the explicit driver ownership model; if overlapping driver calls must be supported, serialize the complete tick before executing effects. Merely replacing swap\"'! with reset! does not make concurrent ticks safe. Add a meaningful dial regression demonstrating that a cursor commit conflict cannot re-execute append! or multiply answer writes.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Checkpoint assessment\\\\n\\\\n| Checkpoint | Assessment and citations |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| Budget exhaustion preserves continuation | PASS. Zero remaining returns the current opaque cursor before another read, with no fabricated answer/end (\"'`remote.cljc:298-301`). Successful reads adopt the returned successor cursor (`:314`); gaps adopt the source recovery cursor (`:317`). |'\"\\\\n| Malformed reads and gaps count | PASS. Every ok branch and gap branch recurs with decremented remaining; junk and answer-shaped values consume allowance too (\"'`remote.cljc:301-317`). Blocked/end return without recurring (`:315-316`). |'\"\\\\n| Chase clamp and absent request budget | PASS by inspection and focused tests. Chase requires next, a positive request budget, and an initial ok; its allowance is min(peer, local) (\"'`remote.cljc:236-243`). Without a peer budget it performs no chase. The initial next counts toward k, so clamp 3 yields at most two more outcomes (`:135-151`). |'\"\\\\n| Writer full on idempotent requests | PASS in the remote loop. Returned writer outcome reaches the full check; descriptor, cursor, next and named descriptor stop with the preceding cursor (\"'`remote.cljc:197-204,223-249,305-314`). Oversize replacement'\"'\\\\''s full outcome also propagates (\"'`:161-169`). |'\"\\\\n| Writer full on append\"'! | PASS in the remote loop. append! explicitly bypasses rewind and advances (`remote.cljc:310-314`); the new test proves one source append over sequential ticks (`remote_test.cljc:1762-1777`). Composition retry safety fails R1. |'\"\\\\n| Invalid bounds | PASS. Non-nil non-map bounds and any non-positive/non-integer non-nil map value throw the specified ex-info before channel reads/writes (\"'`remote.cljc:289-295`). Acceptor and dial validate/store their new keys (`ws_project.cljc:211-243,459-488`). |'\"\\\\n| Effects outside atom retry | FAIL at dial-step\"'!, R1. Acceptor mirror execution is outside the state update (`ws_project.cljc:389-401`). |'\"\\\\n| Backward arities/defaults | PASS for budget/chase behavior. Four/five arities delegate with nil (\"'`remote.cljc:285-288`); nil remaining is unbounded and nil chase-max preserves peer allowance. Writer-full rewind is the intentional specified behavior change shared by all arities. |'\"\\\\n| Acceptor/dial wiring | PASS. Acceptor passes both mirror bounds (\"'`ws_project.cljc:391-396`); dial passes step-budget to projection and both mirror bounds (`:582-590`). New integration tests exercise continuation over multiple ticks. |'\"\\\\n| Documentation | Matches implemented S2a signatures, counting, clamp and full handling (\"'`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:193-257,425-434`). No additional documentation blocker identified. |'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Non-blocking coverage notes\\\\n\\\\n- New full-writer tests directly cover identity descriptor, named descriptor and append\"'!, but not cursor/next (`remote_test.cljc:1734-1777`). Add cursor/next cases, preferably a noninitial rewind position and a bounded chase, to protect the complete stated idempotent set.'\"\\\\n- The chase test covers local clamps 3 and 20 and nil local bounds, but does not directly exercise local clamp 1 or a request without a peer budget under non-nil local bounds (\"'`remote_test.cljc:1706-1731`). The inspected guards are correct.'\"\\\\n- §1.2 also mentions four S2b/S2c link policy keys and a timed dial-step\"'! arity. Their deferral is documented in the implementer'\"'\\\\''s report and depends on later slices; it is not an S2a defect.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification and limits\\\\n\\\\nIndependently ran the focused JVM tests using the existing test classpath, avoiding CLI cache generation:\\\\n\"'```sh'\"\\\\njava -cp \\\\\\\"\"'$(cat .cpcache/3644903311.cp)'\"\\\\\\\" clojure.main \\\\\\\\\\\\n  -m cognitect.test-runner \\\\\\\\\\\\n  -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test\\\\n\"'```'\"\\\\n**63 tests, 479 assertions, zero failures, zero errors.**\\\\n\\\\nBoth in-memory adversarial reproductions ran on the JVM and observed duplicate source effects as described above. No reproduction or test source file was created. Full JVM suite, Node/Dart lanes and lint were not independently run in this read-only review. The implementer reports focused JVM success and lint success with one preexisting warning, and explicitly leaves full three-host verification outstanding; this review does not certify the D5 all-host landing gate.\\\\n\\\\n## Disposition\\\\n\\\\nResolve R1 in the dial path and rerun focused tests with a regression for effect execution outside retry. The S2a remote budget/rewind implementation and its wiring otherwise conform to the inspected specification. Cross-host landing verification remains required.\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
